# CometGUI -- line endings for the files a Windows runner has to EXECUTE.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  GitHub's windows-latest image installs Git for Windows
# with /VERYSILENT and passes no CRLFOption override -- its
# images/windows/scripts/build/Install-Git.ps1 sets only safe.directory -- so
# the installer default, core.autocrlf=true, is what applies on that runner.
# Under that setting a checked-out shell script arrives with CRLF line endings,
# and Git Bash then runs it with the carriage returns still in it.
#
# That is fatal on the FIRST LINE OF EVERY SCRIPT HERE.  Every scripts/ci/*.sh
# begins with `set -Eeuo pipefail`, and with a trailing \r that line is
# `set -Eeuo pipefail\r`.  Demonstrated on this machine (Linux, GNU bash),
# 2026-08-30, rather than assumed:
#
#     $ printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\nset -Eeuo pipefail\r\necho hi\r\n' > crlf.sh
#     $ bash crlf.sh
#     crlf.sh: line 2: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#     $ echo $?
#     2
#
#   -- while the identical script written with LF prints `hi` and exits 0.  The
# same failure hits every later line: a command name with \r appended is not a
# command, hence the more familiar `$'\r': command not found`.
#
# The rules below remove the dependency on core.autocrlf entirely: these files
# are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform, no
# matter how the person or the runner has Git configured.
#
# THIS ALSO FIXES A LATENT FAILURE THAT ALREADY EXISTED.  The Windows job in
# .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs `bash scripts/ci/nightly-windows-raw.sh`
# and would have hit exactly this wall the first time it ran.  It never has --
# GitHub has executed nothing in this repository -- so the bug has never been
# observed, and it is fixed here before it can be.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT `* text=auto`.  A blanket rule decides line endings for
# every file in the repository by guessing which ones are text, and this
# project ships fixtures whose bytes are pinned by SHA-256.  Naming the two
# extensions that a Windows runner executes is the whole of what is needed.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
